    "description": "Provide the Automation Center of Excellence with a reusable UiPath runtime simulator that converts configuration-driven, agent-generated records into realistic single-job or transactional executions. The simulator exercises Orchestrator assets, queues, stop requests, retries, application and data-source delays, business and system exceptions, structured logs, and UiPath Insights mappings without requiring production system integrations.",
    "execution_model": {
      "classification": "transactional",
      "rationale": "The complete capability processes independent, queue-friendly records through dispatcher and performer entry points. The single-job entry point remains a supported bounded scenario of the same capability.",
      "queueing_recommendation": "Use transactional execution for volume, retry, and queue-behavior validation. Use single-job execution for bounded demonstrations."
    }
  },
